# Per-org GitHub token map for the repo audit suite.
#
# One line per org: "<org> <ENV_VAR_NAME>". When an audit target's GitHub org
# matches an entry here, the wrappers (gh-read, repo-fetch) use the named
# environment variable as GH_TOKEN instead of gh's normal authentication —
# useful when different orgs need different tokens (e.g. separate identities
# per GitHub Enterprise install). An unmapped org falls back to gh's normal
# auth. Unset lines are ignored.
#
# Copy this file to the location named by the `token_map` config key
# (default ~/.claude/plugins/data/crew/token-map), edit it for your orgs, and
# export the named variables in your shell before running an audit. Never
# commit a real token-map with live org names next to real tokens.

example-org GITHUB_TOKEN_EXAMPLE_ORG
